================================================================================================
(3) BRICK (B) EXACT REDUCTION: what Var-bound gives D3 >= bar, over R2 <= 614?
================================================================================================
  D3 >= PZ = 1/(1 + Var/E[W]^2);  PZ >= bar  <=>  Var <= (1/bar - 1)*E[W]^2
  (1/bar - 1) = 2.0192;  so need Var <= 2.0192 * E[W]^2
  min E[W] over compact k=11 (diam<=16): 0.14360 at [0, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 16]
  => Var <= 0.04164 suffices for PZ>=bar (hence D3>=bar).
     With Var <= c*R2 (c~5.67e-5) and R2<=614: Var <= 0.03481
     PZ>=bar needs Var <= 0.04164: HOLDS (brick B via PZ closes)
  [D3 > PZ gives MORE room; the exact D3>=bar threshold is looser than the PZ one above.]
